Now I understand the flow. The fuzzer calls:
1. Mat_VarReadNextInfo - reads variable info (dimensions, class, etc.)
2. Mat_VarReadDataAll - calls ReadData -> Mat_VarRead5

For numeric types in Mat_VarRead5, the function just seeks to datapos and sets data_size/data_type. The actual data reading happens through Mat_VarReadData5 which is called from Mat_VarReadDataAll.

Wait, let me re-read the fuzzer:
```cpp
while ((matvar = Mat_VarReadNextInfo(matfd)) != nullptr) {
    Mat_VarReadDataAll(matfd, matvar);
    ...
}
```

Mat_VarReadDataAll calls ReadData which calls Mat_VarRead5. So for numeric types, Mat_VarRead5 doesn't allocate data. Let me check what happens for numeric types in Mat_VarRead5 more carefully...

Actually, looking at Mat_VarRead5 for MAT_C_DOUBLE:
```c
case MAT_C_DOUBLE:
    (void)fseek((FILE*)mat->fp,matvar->internal->datapos,SEEK_SET);
    matvar->data_size = sizeof(double);
    matvar->data_type = MAT_T_DOUBLE;
    break;
```

It just seeks to datapos and sets data_size/data_type. It doesn't allocate data or read anything. So for numeric types, Mat_VarReadDataAll doesn't actually read the data into matvar->data. The data is only read when Mat_VarReadData5 is called with a pre-allocated buffer.

